          <msContents>
            <summary>[p]Medical compendium[/p]

[p][b]Contents[/b][/p]

[p]1. ff. 1r-2r [i]De anima[/i][/p]

[p]f. 1r Anima vegetiva non est una ... f. 2r ... et sic per accidens.[/p]

[p]2. ff. 2r-8v Notes in several fifteenth-century hands on medical recipes and physic.[/p]

[p]f. 2r Illud est rarius alio quod sub equali ... [/p]

[p]3. ff. 9r-11r [i]Virtutes aque vite[/i], probably based on Arnold of Villanova[/p]

[p]f. 9r Hec sunt virtutes aque vitis sive ardentis. Si capilli in radicibus frequenter ... f. 11r ... et sine aliqua lesione.[/p]

[p]4. f. 11r [i]De saporibus[/i][/p]

[p]f. 11r Novem sunt sapores scilicet dulcis amarus ... et acetus fit a minora.[/p]

[p]5. f. 11v Schema on the non-naturals[/p]

[p]6. ff. 12r-14v 21 canons on pharmacy[/p]

[p]f. 12r In hoc 4o capitulo postquam in presenti posui canones universales ... f. 14v ... farmacies purgan difficile.[/p]

[p]7. ff. 15r-19v Albert the Great, [i]Experimenta[/i][/p]

[p]f. 15r Omnis sciencia de genere bonorum est ...  f. 19v ... ad interrogationem si perpetravit.[/p]

[p]8. ff. 20r-v A short description of magnes and a [i]probatio pennae[/i] in Italian[/p]

[p]9. ff. 21r-34v Hippocrates, [i]Aphorisms[/i], incomplete[/p]

[p]f. 21r Ypocrates in prima particula afforismorum. Vita brevis ars vero longa ... f. 34v ... quam corporis motio turbat.[/p]

[p]ff. 35r-37v blank[/p]

[p]10. ff. 38r-48v Theophilus of Ferrara, [i]Propositiones ex libro physici[/i][/p]

[p]f. 38r Incipiunt Auctoritates ... primi libri. Scire et intelligere contingit circa omnes sciencias ... f. 48v ... per se sed per formam.[/p]

[p]11. ff. 49r-58r Canons, chapters 6, 1-20-25, on purging[/p]

[p]f. 49r Capitulum 6m. Positis canonibus attendentis in euvactione ... f. 58r ... aut flegmaticorum in crudationem.[/p]</summary>
